      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e validation and setting ofpvmfw load address seems a bit unrelated to rest of the arch.* fields we set here(compared to arch.pkvm.pvmfw_load_addr)\n\nWhy? The very idea is that pvmfw_load_addr is just like any other VM params that are initialized post VM init, pre vCPUs creation.\n\n\u003e something like pkvm_validate_pvmfw_load_addr() which validates and sets kvm-\u003earch.pkvm.pvmfw_load_addr?\n\nFor other params, we first validate them all, then (once we know they all are valid) set them all, in a unified fashion. Why do it differently for pvmfw_load_addr?\n\nIf we validate and set pvmfw_load_addr _after_ validating and setting other params, it means that if pvmfw_load_addr validation fails, even though vCPU creation fails, we leave a side effect on the VM state. Similarly if we validate and set pvmfw_load_addr  _before_ validating and setting other params. Even if this side effect is not harmful, it\u0027s still cleaner to avoid it?",
      "parentUuid": "f669d1dc_d1ea6693",
      "revId": "a875c2229201c574ec9bde066049b9b19da48076",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
